#! Go to definition (s133), under the facsimile profile: a cross-file item
#! (`geometry.area` -> the sibling module's `pub fn area`, at a URI this
#! client never opened), the module name itself (a directory: its first
#! file, at the top), a local through an f-string interpolation, and a
#! prelude name (`print`: null, never an error). The answer's SHAPE is the
#! profile's own claim — `LocationLink[]` where the client declares
#! `linkSupport`, `Location[]` where it does not — which is why there is
#! one of these per client and they are not copies.
name      navigation/definition-facsimile
profile   facsimile

initialize
open      resolve/two_mod/main.lu
wait      diagnostics resolve/two_mod/main.lu
req       definition resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:16
req       definition resolve/two_mod/main.lu 11:7
open      hello.lu
wait      diagnostics hello.lu
req       definition hello.lu 10:19
req       definition hello.lu 10:4
shutdown
